511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1152 0 R
/E (The costs are derived from calculations that account for monthly manpower hours used which are not reflective of actual salaried employees as they are paid on a monthly basis regardless of the productive manpower hours in a given month)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1153 0 R
/E (The LP optimal model suggests an increase and decrease in manpower that mimics a chase strategy for some portions which is not realistic given the time to train new employees, hit to employer reputation and lack of operational stability for a given department)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1154 0 R
/E (The LP optimal minimizes total cost but does not prioritize balanced workforce utilization. As a result, periods of increased staffing may still require overtime which reduces the operational benefits of workforce expansion)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
514 0 obj
<<
